Distributed Databases and NoSQL

Relational databases are powerful but can struggle with extremely large or unstructured data.

NoSQL databases provide:

Flexible structure

Better scalability

Faster performance for large datasets

Examples:

MongoDB (Document database)

Cassandra (Distributed database)

DynamoDB (Key-value database)

